{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/4/codegen_prompts/8.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/4`\n- 题号：`8`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/4/8.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"8\">\n- `description`：将网格中每个由围墙封闭的房间内的彩色种子像素进行\"生长\"，生长方向由房间墙壁上的门洞位置决定，种子沿门洞的反方向填满房间。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个由 grey 像素围成的封闭矩形\"房间\"，房间内部为背景色。\n  - 每个房间的墙壁上恰好有一个单像素宽的缺口（\"门洞\"），门洞位置在四面墙的某一面上。\n  - 每个房间内部恰好有一个非背景色、非 grey 的彩色种子像素，种子像素紧贴房间的某一面内壁。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个房间，确定门洞所在的方向（上、下、左、右）。\n  - 从种子像素开始，用种子的颜色向门洞的对面方向（即远离门洞的方向）填充房间内部：具体地，填充从种子像素所在行/列开始，向门洞反方向扩展，直到碰到对面的墙壁为止，形成一个矩形色块。填充宽度等于房间内部的完整宽度（若门洞在上或下面）或完整高度（若门洞在左或右面）。\n  - 门洞本身保持为背景色（不被填充）。\n  - 房间墙壁和门洞不变，房间外部不变。\n- `Key insight`：直觉上种子可能会\"朝门洞方向生长\"，但实际规则恰恰相反——生长方向背离门洞。解题者需要通过多个样例才能排除\"朝门洞生长\"这个强干扰假设，发现真正的反方向规则。同时，填充范围不是简单的射线，而是占满房间宽度/高度的矩形色块，这也需要从样例中归纳。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/8b7bacbf, train/ac6f9922, train/78e78cff, train/6ca952ad, train/278e5215, train/aa62e3f4, eval/b9e38dc0, eval/3e6067c3\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4123\nmechanism=0.4556\nlexical=0.0129\ncode_feature=0.8333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:closed_region, object:hole, object:marker, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:flood_fill, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ac6f9922\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3752\nmechanism=0.4598\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:closed_region, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/ac6f9922.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ac6f9922.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSummarize the enclosed table slots by the single object color inside each slot, using the slot background color for empty slots.\n\nInput structure\n- The most common color forms the outer background and all enclosed slot\n  backgrounds.\n- The enclosed background components form a complete rectangular array of\n  slots, ordered by their positions.\n- Each slot contains either no other color or exactly one object color.\n\nRule\n- Find all 4-connected components of the most common color that do not touch\n  the input edge.\n- Sort their bounding boxes into row and column order to define the output\n  table.\n- For each slot, output its unique non-background color if present; otherwise\n  output the background color.\n\nKey insight\n- The large grid is an expanded table: the enclosed background components are\n  the cells, and any colored object drawn inside a cell is that cell's summary\n  value.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"enclosed 4-connected background-color slot components arranged as a rectangular table, each containing zero or one non-background object color\",\n  \"transform\": \"collapse each slot to one output pixel in row/column order: use the contained object color if present, otherwise use the background color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"number of slot rows x number of slot columns\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"78e78cff\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3656\nmechanism=0.4750\nlexical=0.0129\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:hole, object:marker, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:flood_fill, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/78e78cff.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/78e78cff.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.\n- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.\n- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.\n\nRule:\n- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly\n  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only\n  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.\n- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.\n- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.\n- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.\n\nKey insight:\n- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the\n  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling\n  through connected background.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one singleton marker pixel and rows of wall-color pixels on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor background pixels in the scanline passage selected by the marker column: wall rows fill between nearest wall limits, empty interior rows fill full width, and empty exterior rows reuse the nearest end interval\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6ca952ad\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3639\nmechanism=0.4431\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:hole, object:marker, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6ca952ad.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6ca952ad.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected foreground objects with area greater than three pixels\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical downward ray in the object's original columns until its bbox bottom touches the grid bottom\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate the whole object once without changing shape or color\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear moved objects at their original positions; leave foreground objects of area at most three pixels fixed\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"278e5215\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2977\nmechanism=0.2860\nlexical=0.0160\ncode_feature=0.8333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:hole, object:rectangle, operation:count, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/278e5215.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/278e5215.json\n</paths>\n<description>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
